hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"8","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, Muhammad bin Jafar told us. H Al-Hussein bin Muhammad Al-Dhari’ narrated to us, Yazid bin Zurayi narrated to us. H Yahya bin Hakim told us, Abu Dawud told us, they all said: Shu`bah told us, and this is the wording of the hadith of Bundar, on the authority of Simak bin Harb, on the authority of Musab bin Saad, who said: Ibn Amir fell ill and they praised him, but Ibn Omar was silent, so he said: I am not deceiving them. But the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “God does not accept a prayer without purification, nor charity from impure things.”"
"9","Al-Hasan bin Saeed Abu Muhammad Al-Qazzaz Al-Farsi narrated to us, he lived in Baghdad, with news with a strange chain of transmission. He said: Ghassan bin Ubaid narrated to us. Al-Mawsili, Ikrimah bin Ammar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No prayer will be accepted except with purification, and no charity will be given from unjust people.”"
"10","Abu Ammar Al-Hasan bin Harith narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz bin Abi Hazim narrated to us, on the authority of many, and he is Ibn Yazid, on the authority of Al-Walid, and he is Ibn Rabah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “God does not accept a prayer without purification, nor alms from deceitful people.”"
